{"type":"message","id":"1550505d","parentId":"51fdcaff","timestamp":"2026-06-16T05:19:58.975Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_00_QdJ8MEq6iVTJxJrJpxvS9950","toolName":"exec","content":[{"type":"text","text":"def calc(self, symbol: str) -> dict:\n        now = time.time()\n        if symbol in self.cache and now - self.cache_ts.get(symbol, 0) < 60:\n            return self.cache[symbol]\n\n        klines_15m = self._get_klines(symbol, \"15m\", 100)\n        klines_1h  = self.get_24h_klines(symbol)\n\n        if not klines_15m:\n            return {}\n\n        closes_15m = [float(k[4]) for k in klines_15m]\n        closes_1h  = [float(k[4]) for k in klines_1h] if klines_1h else closes_15m\n        highs  = [float(k[2]) for k in klines_15m]\n        lows   = [float(k[3]) for k in klines_15m]\n        vols   = [float(k[5]) for k in klines_15m]\n\n        atr = self._atr(klines_15m)\n        price = closes_15m[-1]\n\n        result = {\n            \"last_close\":  price,\n            # RSI\n            \"rsi\":         self._rsi(closes_15m),\n            # EMA 15分钟\n            \"ema20_15m\":   self._ema(closes_15m, 20),\n            \"ema60_15m\":   self._ema(closes_15m, 60),\n            # EMA 1小时（多时间框架确认）\n            \"ema20_1h\":    self._ema(closes_1h, 20),\n            \"ema60_1h\":    self._ema(closes_1h, 60),\n            # 成交量\n            \"vol_current\": vols[-1],\n            \"vol_avg20\":   float(np.mean(vols[-20:])),\n            # ATR\n            \"atr\":         atr,\n            \"atr_pct\":     atr / price if price else 0,\n            # 支撑阻力（20根K线）\n            \"resistance\":  max(highs[-20:]),\n            \"support\":     min(lows[-20:]),\n            # 市场状态原始数据\n            \"ema_slope\":   (closes_15m[-1] - closes_15m[-5]) / closes_15m[-5] if closes_15m[-5] else 0,\n        }\n\n        self.cache[symbol] = result\n        self.cache_ts[symbol] = now\n        return result\n\n\n# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n# 三、市场状态识别（Regime Detection）\n# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════"}],"details":{"status":"completed","exitCode":0,"durationMs":92,"aggregated":"def calc(self, symbol: str) -> dict:\n        now = time.time()\n        if symbol in self.cache and now - self.cache_ts.get(symbol, 0) < 60:\n            return self.cache[symbol]\n\n        klines_15m = self._get_klines(symbol, \"15m\", 100)\n        klines_1h  = self.get_24h_klines(symbol)\n\n        if not klines_15m:\n            return {}\n\n        closes_15m = [float(k[4]) for k in klines_15m]\n        closes_1h  = [float(k[4]) for k in klines_1h] if klines_1h else closes_15m\n        highs  = [float(k[2]) for k in klines_15m]\n        lows   = [float(k[3]) for k in klines_15m]\n        vols   = [float(k[5]) for k in klines_15m]\n\n        atr = self._atr(klines_15m)\n        price = closes_15m[-1]\n\n        result = {\n            \"last_close\":  price,\n            # RSI\n            \"rsi\":         self._rsi(closes_15m),\n            # EMA 15分钟\n            \"ema20_15m\":   self._ema(closes_15m, 20),\n            \"ema60_15m\":   self._ema(closes_15m, 60),\n            # EMA 1小时（多时间框架确认）\n            \"ema20_1h\":    self._ema(closes_1h, 20),\n            \"ema60_1h\":    self._ema(closes_1h, 60),\n            # 成交量\n            \"vol_current\": vols[-1],\n            \"vol_avg20\":   float(np.mean(vols[-20:])),\n            # ATR\n            \"atr\":         atr,\n            \"atr_pct\":     atr / price if price else 0,\n            # 支撑阻力（20根K线）\n            \"resistance\":  max(highs[-20:]),\n            \"support\":     min(lows[-20:]),\n            # 市场状态原始数据\n            \"ema_slope\":   (closes_15m[-1] - closes_15m[-5]) / closes_15m[-5] if closes_15m[-5] else 0,\n        }\n\n        self.cache[symbol] = result\n        self.cache_ts[symbol] = now\n        return result\n\n\n# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n# 三、市场状态识别（Regime Detection）\n# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════","cwd":"/root/.openclaw/workspace"},"isError":false,"timestamp":1781587198963}}
{"type":"message","id":"b5d5a54e","parentId":"1550505d","timestamp":"2026-06-16T05:20:34.370Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I have all the information I need. Let me implement the `update_atr_dynamic_stops` function. Here's my plan:\n\n1. Add the function after `update_trailing_stop` (around line 750, before `_cancel_algo_by_type`)\n2. Add the call site in the main loop after indicators are updated\n\nThe function will:\n- For each position, get the current ATR from indicators\n- Calculate the ATR-based SL (same formula as calc_tp_sl but only for SL)\n- Compare with current SL\n- Update if needed\n\nLet me write the code.\n\nWait, I should also think about whether to update the TP based on ATR. The calc_tp_sl also has ATR-dynamic TP: `tp_pct = max(4%, min(atr_pct * 2.0, 15%))`. Should the TP also be dynamic? \n\nHmm,老公 specifically said \"弹性移动止盈止损倍率\" - both SL and TP. Let me update both.\n\nBut updating TP could be dangerous - if ATR increases, the TP would widen (from 4% to up to 15%), which means the position would need to move further to take profit. That seems counterintuitive during volatile periods. \n\nActually, re-reading the code comment: \"止盈 ATR 动态，崩盘时自动放宽\" - the TP widens during crashes so you don't get taken out too early. That makes sense.\n\nBut for existing positions, should I really widen the TP? If the position was entered with a 4% TP target, and then the market gets volatile, widening to 15% could mean missing the original target entirely.\n\nI think for safety, I should only update the SL based on ATR dynamics, not the TP. Or at most, only allow the TP to tighten (from 15% down), not widen.\n\nActually, let me keep it simple and focused on what老公 asked. He said \"弹性移动止盈止损倍率\" - I'll update both SL and TP dynamically, but only in the favorable direction:\n\nFor SL:\n- ATR dynamic SL from entry → if tighter than current, update. If looser, only update if position hasn't reached trailing Tier 1.\n\nFor TP:\n- ATR dynamic TP from entry → if tighter (closer to entry, easier to hit), update. If looser (further), don't update (keep the original, easier-to-hit target).\n\nActually no, let me re-read the original formula more carefully:\n\nFor SHORT:\n- TP: entry * (1 - tp_pct) where tp_pct = max(4%, min(atr * 2.0, 15%))\n- SL: entry * (1 + sl_pct) where sl_pct = max(2%, min(atr * atr_mult, 15%))\n\nWhen ATR increases:\n- tp_pct increases → TP price moves further away from entry → harder to hit\n- sl_pct increases → SL price moves further from entry → wider stop\n\nWhen ATR decreases:\n- tp_pct stays at 4% minimum → TP stays same\n- sl_pct stays at 2% minimum → SL stays same\n\nSo the dynamics mostly apply in the upward direction (higher ATR → wider everything).\n\nHmm, but the ATR multiplier system is really about setting appropriate risk parameters for the current volatility environment. During entry, it's forward-looking. During holding, it should be continuously adapting.\n\nOK, I'll implement it as follows:\n- For every cycle, calculate current ATR-based SL/TP\n- Update SL: apply the new ATR-based SL, unless the trailing stop has tightened it further (trailing SL is tighter than ATR SL)\n- Update TP: apply the new ATR-based TP (always, since it's about appropriate targeting)\n\nWait, actually for TP updating, I need to be more careful. The TP is set at entry. If ATR increased and we widen the TP, the position might never hit it. Also, the green query output showed the current TP: BNB 607.7 (4% from 633), DOT 0.9734 (4% from 1.014), LINK 7.9363 (4% from 8.267). All are at the 4% base level.\n\nIf I start dynamically adjusting TP based on ATR, it could get weird. Let me focus only on SL for now.\n\nFor SL, the logic:\n```python\ndef update_atr_dynamic_stops(positions, indicators):\n    for pos in positions:\n        sym = pos[\"symbol\"]\n        if sym not in indicators:\n            continue\n        \n        ind = indicators[sym]\n        atr_pct = ind.get(\"atr_pct\", 0)\n        if atr_pct <= 0:\n            continue\n        \n        entry = pos[\"entry_price\"]\n        typ = pos[\"type\"]\n        \n        # Same ATR multiplier as calc_tp_sl\n        atr_mult = 1.0\n        for threshold, mult in CONFIG[\"atr_sl_tiers\"]:\n            if atr_pct < threshold:\n                atr_mult = mult\n                break\n        \n        sl_pct = max(0.02, min(atr_pct * atr_mult, 0.15))\n        \n        if typ == \"LONG\":\n            atr_sl = entry * (1 - sl_pct)\n            # tighter = higher for LONG\n            current_sl = pos[\"sl_price\"]\n            if atr_sl > current_sl:\n                # ATR SL is tighter → update\n                old_sl = current_sl\n                pos[\"sl_price\"] = round(atr_sl, 4)\n                sync_stop_loss_to_binance(sym, typ, pos[\"sl_price\"], old_sl, pos.get(\"tp1_price\", 0), qty=abs(pos.get(\"amount\", 0)))\n        else:\n            atr_sl = entry * (1 + sl_pct)\n            # tighter = lower for SHORT\n            current_sl = pos[\"sl_price\"]\n            if atr_sl < current_sl:\n                old_sl = current_sl\n                pos[\"sl_price\"] = round(atr_sl, 4)\n                sync_stop_loss_to_binance(sym, typ, pos[\"sl_price\"], old_sl, pos.get(\"tp1_price\", 0), qty=abs(pos.get(\"amount\", 0)))\n```\n\nWait, but this only tightens. What about when ATR increases and the SL should widen? The text 老公 emphasized was \"弹性\" which means it should go both ways.\n\nLet me reconsider. When ATR increases:\n- More volatility → wider stops needed\n- If current SL is tight (2% from entry) and ATR is now 5%\n- The recommended SL would be atr_pct * atr_mult = 5% * 2.0 = 10%\n- SL should widen from 2% to 10% from entry\n- For SHORT at 633 entry: SL goes from 617.8 (2.4%) to 696.3 (10%)\n\nBut wait, the current price is 614.1. If we widen SL to 696.3, that's WAY above the current price. That doesn't make sense for a SHORT position.\n\nAlso, the trailing stop might have already decided on an appropriate SL.\n\nI think the right approach is:\n1. Calculate ATR-based SL from entry\n2. Apply it as a NEW SL ONLY IF it's tighter than current (ATR decreased)\n3. IF it's looser than current (ATR increased), only apply if the position hasn't seen significant profit movement (i.e., no trailing tier has activated)\n\nThis way:\n- In calm markets → SL tightens\n- In volatile markets → SL widens IF we're not in profit, protecting from stop-outs\n- In volatile markets + in profit → trailing stop keeps the tighter SL\n\nLet me implement this. Actually, let me simplify even more:\n\nFor each position:\n1. Calculate ATR-based recommended SL (from entry price)\n2. Check if trailing stop has ever tightened the SL (peak_pnl >= first tier threshold)\n3. If trailing stop active → skip (trailing is in control)\n4. If no trailing active → update SL to ATR-based recommendation\n\nThis keeps it simple and non-conflicting with the trailing stop.\n\nLet me code this up now.\n\nActually wait, there's one more thing to consider. The current SL is already in `pos[\"sl_price\"]`. It might have been set at entry time OR modified by trailing stop. If modified by trailing stop, we should respect that.\n\nThe simplest rule: \n- Only update SL based on ATR if the position hasn't reached any trailing tier (peak_pnl < tp_pct * first_tier_ratio)\n- In that case, always update to current ATR-based SL\n\nLet me implement this. The first tier threshold from SOUL.md is 2% of tp_pct. In code terms: `peak_pnl < tp_pct * CONFIG[\"trailing_tiers\"][0][\"pnl_ratio\"]`.\n\nActually, looking at the CONFIG again:\n```python\n\"trailing_tiers\": [\n    # tier format: (pnl_ratio, gap_ratio)... let me check the actual config\n```\n\nLet me look at the actual CONFIG to see the tier format.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_00_ThGoDx2ZNNvKsPINRdiF6524","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"cd ~/.openclaw/workspace/scripts && sed -n '80,100p' crypto_s