{"type":"message","id":"766471c9","parentId":"edaf932d","timestamp":"2026-06-16T11:34:02.388Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"BNB SL is still 0.0 and peak_price is 0. My manual fix to crypto_positions.json was overwritten on restart. Let me investigate why.\n\nThe startup code path:\n1. API returns 3 positions\n2. old_positions = load_positions() → reads crypto_positions.json\n3. But I already had manually set BNB SL=617.81 and peak_price=611.69\n4. old_map should have BNB with these values\n5. For BNB: old_sl=617.81, new_sl=645.66\n6. SHORT: tighter = 617.81 < 645.66 → True\n7. So sl_price = old_sl = 617.81\n8. peak_price = old.get(\"peak_price\", 0) = 611.69\n\nBut the result shows SL=0.0 and peak_price=0. So the old_positions didn't have my manual fix?\n\nWait, let me check the file order. The `submit_initial_algo_orders` function at line 877 checks `if not sl_price or not tp_price: return`. And BNB shows TP exists (607.7) but SL doesn't. \n\nActually, let me re-read the submit_initial_algo_orders flow. After the position rebuild, there's:\n1. Orphan cleanup\n2. `for pos in positions: submit_initial_algo_orders(pos)`\n\nLooking at submit_initial_algo_orders:\n```python\nsl_price = pos.get(\"sl_price\")\ntp_price = pos.get(\"tp1_price\")\nif not sl_price or not tp_price:\n    return\n```\n\nIf sl_price is 617.81 and tp_price is 607.69, both are truthy, so it should proceed to submit both.\n\nBut the result shows SL=0.0 in the file and no SL on Binance. So something after the position rebuild sets SL back to 0.\n\nWait, let me look at the code flow again more carefully. After the position rebuild section:\n```python\nsave_positions(positions)\n```\n\nThen orphan cleanup, submit_initial_algo_orders.\n\nThen:\n```python\n# 应用恢复的 peak_pnl 到持仓（移动止盈关键数据）\nif peak_pnl_map and positions:\n    for pos in positions:\n        sym = pos[\"symbol\"]\n        if sym in peak_pnl_map:\n            pos[\"peak_pnl\"] = peak_pnl_map[sym]\n   