t me think about this differently. Maybe `load_positions` strips USDT suffix. Or maybe the JSON file doesn't actually have USDT.\n\nYou know what, let me just check the actual file content directly.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_00_EKpU0RNlBnEpOfflD4QP8691","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"cd ~/.openclaw/workspace/scripts && python3 -c \"\nimport json\ndata = json.loads(open('crypto_positions.json').read())\nprint(json.dumps([{k: v for k,v in p.items() if k in ['symbol','sl_price','tp1_price','peak_pnl','peak_price','tp_pct','type']} for p in data], indent=2))\n\" 2>&1","timeout":5}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"deepseek","model":"deepseek-v4-pro","usage":{"input":393,"output":4414,"cacheRead":68736,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":73543,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1781609606007}}
