e was overwritten.\n\nActually, I think there might be a race condition. Let me check if old_positions properly loaded my fix.\n\nActually wait, let me look at the startup code flow again. The code path is:\n\n```python\napi_positions = get_all_positions()\nif not api_positions:\n    ...load from file...\nelse:\n    old_positions = load_positions()\n    old_map = {p.get(\"symbol\", \"\"): p for p in old_positions}\n    ...\n    for p in api_positions:\n        amt = float(p.get('amount', 0))\n        entry = float(p.get('entry_price', 0))\n        if amt != 0 and abs(amt) * entry >= 5.0:\n            symbol = p['symbol']\n            ...\n            old = old_map.get(symbol, {})\n            old_direction = old.get(\"type\", \"\")\n            ...\n```\n\nFor BNB: symbol=\"BNB\", old_map should have \"BNB\" as key (from manual fix).\n\nLet me check: what if old_positions was loaded correctly with my fix, but then the code somehow fails?\n\nLet me trace the exact flow for BNB:\n1. entry = 633.01\n2. direction = 'SHORT'\n3. old = old_map.get(\"BNB\", {}) → should return BNB data with SL=617.81\n4. new_tp_sl = calc_tp_sl(633.01, 'SHORT', {}, {}) → SL=645.66, TP=607.68\n5. old_sl = 617.81, new_sl = 645.66\n6. old_direction = \"SHORT\", direction = \"SHORT\" → match\n7. tighter = 617.81 < 645.66 → True\n8. sl_price = 617.81\n9. peak_price = old.get(\"peak_price\", 0) = 611.69\n\nSo the pos dict should have sl_price=617.81. But the file has 0.0.\n\nUnless... there's an exception happening in the position rebuild code that rolls back to the old file. Let me check the except block:\n\n```python\nexcept Exception as e:\n    log.error(f\"❌ 持仓同步失败：{e}\")\n    positions = load_positions()  # 回退到本地文件\n```\n\nIf an exception occurs, it loads from the file. But the file might have been the OLD broken version (before my fix took effect), or the fix was in place.\n\nActually, I think there might be an issue with the try/except. Let me check if the `except` block covers the entire position rebuild or just part of it.\n\nLet me look at the try/except boundaries more carefully.\n\nActually, let me just look at the error log to see if there's an exception.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_00_gP70IdraVUgZvb9wGhCN8981","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"cd ~/.openclaw/workspace/scripts && python3 -c \"\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfrom datetime import datetime\n\n# Try to find recent monitor logs\nimport subprocess\n# check for any recent log files\nresult = subprocess.run('find /tmp -name \\\"*monitor*\\\" -o -name \\\"*crypto*log*\\\" 2>/dev/null | head -10', shell=True, capture_output=True, text=True)\nprint('log files:', result.stdout)\n\n# check stderr from monitor launch script\nkj_result = subprocess.run('cat ~/.openclaw/workspace/scripts/crypto_positions.json', shell=True, capture_output=True, text=True)\nlines = kj_result.stdout.strip().split('\\n')\n# find BNB entry\nfor i, line in enumerate(lines):\n    if 'BNB' in line:\n        print(f'Line {i}: {line}')\n    elif 'sl_price' in line.lower() and i < 50:\n        print(f'Line {i}: {line}')\n\" 2>&1","timeout":10}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"deepseek","model":"deepseek-v4-pro","usage":{"input":375,"output":2549,"cacheRead":73088,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":76012,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1781609679177}}
