{"type":"message","id":"37c15069","parentId":"f5f9b966","timestamp":"2026-06-16T11:36:08.938Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"OK, that function doesn't modify SL. Let me think about this differently.\n\nMaybe the issue is that the OLD startup code (before my fix) was running during the restart. When老公 did `kj`, the old monitor was killed but the new code was loaded. Let me verify that the current file on disk has my startup fix.\n\nWait, I already verified the syntax check passes. The file on disk has my changes. But let me double check: does the startup code section actually contain my fix?\n\nActually, let me trace through the exact flow once more carefully.\n\n1. When the monitor starts:\n   a. `api_positions = get_all_positions()` → returns 3 positions (BNB, DOT, LINK)\n   b. Since api_positions is not empty, goes to the `else` branch\n   c. `old_positions = load_positions()` → reads crypto_positions.json with my fix (BNB SL=617.81)\n   d. `old_map = {\"DOT\": {...}, \"BNB\": {sl_price:617.81,...}, \"LINK\": {...}}`\n   e. Loop through api_positions:\n      - For BNB: old = old_map.get(\"BNB\", {}) → should return the BNB data\n      - old_direction = old.get(\"type\", \"\") → \"SHORT\"\n      - direction = \"SHORT\"\n      - old_sl = 617.81\n      - new_sl from calc_tp_sl = 645.66\n      - tighter = 617.81 < 645.66 → True\n      - sl_price = 617.81\n      - peak_price = old.get(\"peak_price\", 0) = 611.69\n   f. Position is created with sl_price=617.81, peak_price=611.69\n   g. `save_positions(positions)` → writes to file with correct values\n   h. `submit_initial_algo_orders(pos)` for each position\n\nIf this flow executes correctly, the file should have BNB SL=617.81.\n\nBut the result is SL=0.0. Something is going wrong.\n\nPossible issues:\n1. The try/except catches an exception and falls back to `load_positions()` from file\n2. Something in the code between step g and the second save overwrites the file\n3. The `submit_initial_algo_orders` modifies pos data\n\nLet me check possibility 3 - maybe `submit_initial_algo_orders` has a side effect.\n\nActually, let me look at the save/restore flow more carefully:\n\nAfter position rebuild (step g):\n```python\nsave_positions(positions)\n```\n\nThen orphan cleanup and submit_initial_algo_orders. Then:\n\n```python\n# 🔧 2026-06-06 修复：启动时清理不属于任何持仓的孤儿 Algo 条件单\nif AUTO_TRADE_ENABLED:\n    ...orphan cleanup...\n\n# 🐛 仓位反转修复：启动时为从 API 同步的每个持仓提交止盈止损 Algo 单\nfor pos in positions:\n    submit_initial_algo_orders(pos)\n```\n\nThen:\n```python\n# 从状态文件恢复...\nlast_report_hour = ...\npeak_pnl_map = ...\n\n# 应用恢复的 peak_pnl 到持仓\nif peak_pnl_map and positions:\n    for pos in positions:\n        sym = pos[\"symbol\"]\n        if sym in peak_pnl_map:\n            pos[\"peak_pnl\"] = peak_pnl_map[sym]\n    save_positions(positions)  # ← SECOND save, only modifies peak_pnl\n```\n\nThis second save only changes peak_pnl, not sl_price. So this shouldn't be the issue.\n\nLet me consider possibility 1: an exception occurs in the position rebuild code that causes fallback to `load_positions()`.\n\nWhat could throw? \n- `calc_tp_sl(entry, direction, {}, {})` - unlikely to throw\n- `old.get(\"sl_price\", 0)` - simple dict access, won't throw\n- `datetime.now().isoformat()` - won't throw\n\nWait, could there be an issue with `old_positions` being a list of dicts but `old.get()` returning unexpected types? Let me check: if BNB's entry in old_positions has `type: \"SHORT\"`, then `old_direction = \"SHORT\"` and it matches `direction = \"SHORT\"`.\n\nBut what if `old` is an empty dict (because old_map doesn't have \"BNB\" as key)? Then:\n- old_direction = \"\" → doesn't match \"SHORT\"\n- Falls through to using new_sl = 645.66\n- peak_price = 0, peak_pnl = 0\n- sl_price = 645.66\n\nBut the file shows SL=0.0, not 645.66. So the SL is being set to 0 somewhere after the position is created with sl_price=645.66.\n\nHmm, wait. Let me think about this from a different 