gh it goes to /dev/null)\n\nBut since the current SL in the file is 0.0 (and I know old_sl=0 causes the skip), let me modify the startup code to handle the case where old_sl==0 but old data exists with peak_pnl (meaning the SL was lost but we have other valid data).\n\nWait, actually, the deeper issue might be that when the first kj with my \"fix\" ran, the old_positions already had BNB SL=0.0 (from the previous broken restart), and since old_sl=0, the code skipped the restoration. Then the new process also saves with SL=0... but wait, calc_tp_sl should give SL=645.67, not 0.0.\n\nUnless calc_tp_sl actually returns SL=0.0 for some reason? Let me verify.\n\nFrom my test above: `calc_tp_sl: SL=645.6702 TP=607.6896`. So calc_tp_sl works correctly.\n\nBut the file has SL=0.0. Something is setting it to 0 after calc_tp_sl.\n\nHmm, wait. Maybe the issue is that save_positions was called, but then positions were modified in-memory (by submit_initial_algo_orders somehow), and then another save happened that wrote 0 for SL.\n\nActually, let me look at the sequence more carefully:\n\n```python\nsave_positions(positions)  # saves with SL=645.67\n# ... orphan cleanup ...\nfor pos in positions:\n    submit_initial_algo_orders(pos)\n# ... peak_pnl_map restore ...\nsave_positions(positions)  # saves again, only peak_pnl modified\n```\n\nBetween the first save and the second, `submit_initial_algo_orders` runs. Let me check if it modifies `pos[\"sl_price\"]`.\n\nWait, I know! Maybe `submit_initial_algo_orders` fails for BNB (maybe the Binance API rejects the order), and in the error handling, it sets sl_price to 0 or removes it.\n\nLet me look at submit_initial_algo_orders more carefully.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_00_EB1lDRrWE0rQ7R7gV9DU1774","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"cd ~/.openclaw/workspace/scripts && sed -n '877,950p' crypto_signal_monitor.py","timeout":5}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"deepseek","model":"deepsee