{"type":"message","id":"9d4aae01","parentId":"cd4fa13f","timestamp":"2026-06-16T11:38:33.054Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Hmm, BNB still doesn't show a stop loss in the query output. Wait, it does show TP but no SL. Let me check the query_positions.py more carefully. Maybe it only shows SL when there's a specific condition.\n\nActually looking at the output more carefully:\n- DOT: shows both TP and SL\n- BNB: shows only TP (no SL)\n- LINK: shows both TP and SL\n\nLet me check the query_positions code to see what condition determines whether SL is shown. It might be that the SL is only shown when it's calculated from a certain source.\n\nBut actually, let me check - the SL IS on Binance now (I just created it). The query_positions.py might not be reflecting it correctly. Let me verify directly.\n\nActually, the query_positions shows `🛑止损` on DOT and LINK but not BNB. This could be because:\n1. The local file still has issues with BNB\n2. The SL display in query_positions depends on local file data\n\nLet me check the local file one more time.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"BNB 的 🛑止损没显示出来，但 Binance 上已经有了。让我确认一下本地文件和线上一致："},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_00_NPplVgR5MJrHzeSYRtkS1491","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"cd ~/.openclaw/workspace/scripts && python3 -c \"\nimport json\ndata = json.loads(open('crypto_positions.json').read())\nfor p in data:\n    print(f'{p[\\\"symbol\\\"]}: SL={p.get(\\\"sl_price\\\")} TP={p.get(\\\"tp1_price\\\")} peak_pnl={p.get(\\\"peak_pnl\\\",0):.4%} peak_price={p.get(\\\"peak_price\\\")}')\n\" && echo '---' && python3 -c \"\nfrom query_positions import fetch_open_algo_orders\nalgos = fetch_open_algo_orders()\nfor a in algos:\n    if a.get('algoStatus')=='NEW':\n        print(f'{a[\\\"orderType\\\"]} {a[\\\"symbol\\\"]} triggerPrice={a.get(\\\"triggerPrice\\\")}')\n\" 2>/dev/null","timeout":20}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"deepseek","model":"deep