{"type":"message","id":"284d615b","parentId":"dc9ddb04","timestamp":"2026-06-16T11:38:49.906Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The local file still has BNB SL=0.0, even though I just wrote 617.81 to it! The file must have been overwritten by the running monitor process.\n\nThe monitor is running and saves positions periodically (every cycle with save_positions in the main loop). It has the old in-memory data (SL=0.0, peak_price=0) and overwrites my fix.\n\nLet me fix this differently: kill the monitor, fix the file, then restart. 老公 needs to do the kj.\n\nActually wait, let me check: the file was written (I verified it earlier with \"修复前: SL=0.0 peak_price=0 → 修复后: SL=617.81 peak_price=611.69\"). But then the running monitor's save overwrote it back to 0.\n\nI need to:\n1. Tell 老公 the full situation\n2. Fix the file WHILE the monitor is stopped\n3. Then start the monitor with the corrected file\n\nThe safest approach:\n1. Kill monitor\n2. Fix file\n3. Start monitor\n4. Monitor starts with correct data → preserves SL → syncs to Binance\n\nBut I need老公 to do this since I shouldn't initiate destructive operations without permission. Let me tell him the situation and what to do.\n\nActually, I think there's a simpler way. Since the BNB Algo order IS on Binance (I created it directly), and the monitor periodically syncs from API... but the API sync only syncs positions (entry price, amount), not Algo orders. So the Algo order will stay on Binance but the monitor's local file won't reflect it.\n\nThe real fix is: stop monitor → fix file → restart monitor. Let me tell 老公.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"文件在我写完后又被运行中的 monitor 覆盖回去了——它内存里还是旧数据。\n\n现在 Binance 上 BNB 止损单已经在（617.8），但本地文件跟不上。需要 `kj` 重启让它重新读盘：\n\n1. `kj` 杀掉 → 我趁机写入正确数据 → monitor 启动读到修复后的文件 → 三档继续跑\n\n要我直接操作吗？停了 → 修 → 启动，一气呵成 👑"}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"deepseek","model":"deepseek-v4-pro","usage":{"input":259,"output":833,"cach